From 791d6c5b15897c6c4dadeac0a3d70d0fc4925bb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:58:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Cladach: engrave the six words on the harbour wall in Aonchlo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the ogham standing stones with engravings cut into the wall:
Neart, Misneach and Fearg on the top riser; Cineáltas, Trócaire and
Foighne on the foot riser (visible at ebb). Tap-to-read behaviour is
kept (stand below a word); the moon tile now shows a chisel icon.

- oghamMarks.js -> wallEngravings.js (Aonchlo text baked per word,
  laid along the riser face with PGR's affine helper)
- harbourWall: keepClear option so ironwork avoids the words
- tideWater: drop the unused ogham option
- skye_gen: remove the solid stone tiles; maps regenerate identically
- fix stale Uathach/"her" comments (Conall now meets the boat)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E24zVp1VxoDYaBCxjaF3AX
